// See Debug.xcconfig for why the Pods include comes first and why it is
// optional. Profile builds use this file too: the Podfile maps
// 'Profile' => :release, and both configurations take Release.xcconfig as
// their base.
#include? "Pods/Target Support Files/Pods-Runner/Pods-Runner.release.xcconfig"
#include "Generated.xcconfig"

// The signing settings, when there are any. OPTIONAL and gitignored: a team id
// is machine-specific configuration, and a committed one pins the repo to one
// Apple Developer account — the next person clones it and Xcode tries to sign
// against a team they are not in.
//
// It has to arrive HERE rather than through `XCODE_XCCONFIG_FILE`, which
// applies to every target in the workspace: the pods and the SwiftPM packages
// refuse a provisioning profile outright, and the archive fails with
// "flutter_local_notifications does not support provisioning profiles". This
// file is Runner's.
//
// And it has to arrive through an INCLUDE rather than an append, because
// `tools/release.sh` refuses to build a dirty tree — the tag has to name what
// was built. Appending here would fail that check before anything compiled.
//
// Copy `Signing.xcconfig.example` and fill it in to export locally.
#include? "Signing.xcconfig"
